## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### ❌ Unnecessary Re-renders
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create objects in render
function Component({ data }) {
  return (
    <div style={{ color: 'red' }}> {/* ❌ New object on every render */}
      {data.name}
    </div>
  );
}

// ✅ Use constants or useMemo
const styles = { color: 'red' };
function Component({ data }) {
  return <div style={styles}>{data.name}</div>;
}
```

### ❌ Memory Leaks
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T forget to cleanup
useEffect(() => {
  const interval = setInterval(() => {
    // Do something
  }, 1000);
  
  // ❌ Missing cleanup
}, []);

// ✅ Proper cleanup
useEffect(() => {
  const interval = setInterval(() => {
    // Do something
  }, 1000);
  
  return () => clearInterval(interval);
}, []);
```

### ❌ Inefficient Queries
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T fetch all data when you only need some
const { data } = useQuery(['participants'], () => 
  fetch('/api/participants') // ❌ Fetches all participants
);

// ✅ Fetch only what you need
const { data } = useQuery(['participants', { region }], () => 
  fetch(`/api/participants?region=${region}`) // ✅ Fetches filtered data
);
```

